515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (According to QUAST, an analyzer of the genome assembly quality, the best assembly would have been the one which was obtained from Ilumina and done in SPAdes. We can clearly see it in the circos plot from one look. This can be due to several factors: )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 691 0 R
/E (For starters, Nanopore has a higher error rate than ilumina, making it easier for an incorrect assembly. However as we saw, the quality of the reads was good, so this should not be the problem.  )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 692 0 R
/E (Another thing to take into account is the fact that FLYE has a tendency to produce assemblies which are more complete, but with a higher chance of making incorrect rearrangements, while SPAdes tries to produce more fragmented but accurate assemblies. )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 693 0 R
/E (As we can see in the QUAST analysis, the number of missasemblies is considerably higher in the FLYE than in the SPAdes, indicating that the genome has been assembled incorrectly or that the genome is fragmented. )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 694 0 R
/E (Another thing that indicates us that the assembly has not been the best is the high number of mismatches and indels in FLYE, telling us that there have been substantial errors in the assembly that need to be polish for a better result in this assembler. )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
